<section class="citations-section" id="citations">
  <div class="container">
    <h3 class="citations-heading">Sources</h3>
    <ol class="citations-list">
      <li><strong>PEP conformance.</strong> Every competitor score is officially published in the <a href="https://github.com/python/typing/tree/main/conformance/results" target="_blank" rel="noopener">python/typing conformance results</a> (a folder per tool: <a href="https://github.com/python/typing/tree/main/conformance/results/pyright" target="_blank" rel="noopener">pyright</a>, <a href="https://github.com/python/typing/tree/main/conformance/results/mypy" target="_blank" rel="noopener">mypy</a>, <a href="https://github.com/python/typing/tree/main/conformance/results/ty" target="_blank" rel="noopener">ty</a>, <a href="https://github.com/python/typing/tree/main/conformance/results/pyrefly" target="_blank" rel="noopener">pyrefly</a>, <a href="https://github.com/python/typing/tree/main/conformance/results/zuban" target="_blank" rel="noopener">zuban</a>). We link the live results rather than restate a figure, because those scores change as the tools improve. Basilisk&rsquo;s {{ conformance.scorePct }}% ({{ conformance.pass }}/{{ conformance.total }}) is <em>self-measured</em> by running the unmodified <a href="https://github.com/python/typing/tree/{{ conformance.pinnedRef }}/conformance" target="_blank" rel="noopener">python/typing scorer at commit <code>{{ conformance.pinnedRefShort }}</code></a> on our own binary &mdash; Basilisk is not yet in the official published results, so its number is a self-measurement and is not graded on the same run as the tools above.</li>
